From 929df918ebe33593566186f58d78abf1d91e991a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:01:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] BACKPORT: sched/uclamp: add utilization clamping support

Android's ADPF and the Power HAL hand per-task performance hints to the
kernel through sched_setattr() with SCHED_FLAG_UTIL_CLAMP_MIN/_MAX. This
Exynos9820/9825 Linux 4.14.356 tree had none of the uclamp machinery, so
__sched_setscheduler() rejected every such call and the ROM fell back to
its own heuristics.

Port the upstream 5.4 utilization clamping framework and keep the
Samsung scheduler integration intact:

- UAPI: sched_util_min/sched_util_max, SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER1,
  SCHED_FLAG_UTIL_CLAMP_MIN/_MAX and SCHED_FLAG_UTIL_CLAMP.
- Per-task state: uclamp_req[] for the userspace request and uclamp[] for
  the effective value after task-group and system-default restrictions.
- Per-rq clamp buckets with fair and RT class accounting, plus schedutil
  application after the Samsung frequency-boost path.
- Correct -1 reset semantics in uclamp_validate() and
  __setscheduler_uclamp(), including the RT 100% uclamp.min default.
- Fix sched_copy_attr() to use access_ok(VERIFY_READ).
- Reset inherited clamps on fork only after SCHED_FLAG_RESET_ON_FORK has
  changed an RT task's policy.
- Cgroup v1 cpu.uclamp.min/max and cpu.uclamp.latency_sensitive support,
  including effective-value propagation from cpu_cgroup_css_online() so
  a fresh child group defaults to uclamp.min=0 instead of inheriting the
  root group's 100% effective minimum.
- Backport the uclamp_tg_restrict() clamping fix from
  0213b7083e81f4acd69db32cb72eb4e5f220329a ("sched/uclamp: Fix
  uclamp_tg_restrict()") and update active tasks for both clamp IDs.
- Force active-task propagation when the root/system defaults change.
- Apply effective clamps to fair EAS capacity/spare checks and
  find_best_target() placement so UCLAMP_MIN/MAX are not limited to
  frequency selection.

Original patch: d062c36c86f72dbf22ab028ca17d6b88d2173a55 by Star-Seven
("sched: backport utilization clamping (uclamp) from 5.4").

Signed-off-by: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>

Author: @Devandroid-bit.
