From 1b191883b7b56e80b5ce7935da07e22950178ba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:01:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] BACKPORT: sched/ems: apply uclamp to Samsung EMS
 placement

The initial uclamp port only fed schedutil, so UCLAMP_MIN/UCLAMP_MAX did
not influence Samsung's EMS energy-aware CPU selection. Clamp the EMS
task utilization helpers and use the effective values in placement:

- ml_task_util_est() and ml_boosted_task_util() now return the effective
  util clamped by uclamp_eff_value(), after the schedtune margin.
- ml_task_attached_cpu_util() accounts the waking task with its clamped
  utilization instead of the raw value.
- find_min_util_cpu() rejects candidates that cannot hold the boosted
  clamp, select_energy_cpu() no longer treats a clamp-raised task as
  zero-util, and calculate_energy() uses the same clamped estimated
  utilization when removing the task from its previous CPU and adding it
  to the target CPU. Do not subtract raw ml_task_util() while adding the
  clamped value.
- prefer_idle_cpu() honors cpu.uclamp.latency_sensitive in addition to
  schedtune prefer-idle.

Based on the Linux v5.4 uclamp semantics and the original d062c36c86f7
backport by Star-Seven.

Signed-off-by: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>

Author: @Devandroid-bit.
---
 kernel/sched/ems/energy.c     |  4 +++-
 kernel/sched/ems/multi_load.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++------
 kernel/sched/ems/st_addon.c   |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

